The statement

    ALTER TABLE good CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_general_ci;

will not change the character set nor the collation of any existing column in the table. The statement will change the default charset and collation of the table, which will be applied as default charset/collation to new columns added to the table. If you want to change the collation of the existing column "col", you need to do:

    ALTER TABLE good MODIFY COLUMN col varchar(512) COLLATE utf8mb4_general_ci;
